shelves that hold several kinds
  The discriminator is self-asserted, and kind decides every obligation after it.
  A shelf that drifts toward its cheapest kind is what this reading shows.
  library — discriminator `doc_type`, 2 documents
        0 catalog
        1 manual
        1 note

file names, against the layout each shelf declares
  A layout names a file at birth and no check reads one afterwards, so this is a
  convention rather than a rule. A generated document is excluded: its name is the
  emitter's, as its content is.
  decisions — `{slug}.md`, 3 documents
      supplied — `{slug}.md` renders the name of 2 of the 3 documents on `decisions`
  library — `{doc_type}-{slug}.md`, 2 documents
      nothing declares it — not one of the 2 documents on `library` can be measured:
      `manual` requires no facet in the `name` role, so `{slug}` has no declared source;
      `note` requires no facet in the `name` role, so `{slug}` has no declared source
  archive — `{slug}.md`, 0 documents
      nothing authored one — no document stands on `archive`, so `{slug}.md` names
      nothing yet
